# Code quality (write + review)

When the user says **«перевір код»**, «перевірка коду», «рев'ю», «ревью», «аудит коду», «review code», or similar: follow `.cursor/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`. **Find and fix.** Do not only report.

When writing any new or changed code, apply this bar plus `azs-watch.mdc` and `AGENTS.md`. Product rules win over generic style.

## Layers

- HTTP/UI (`Handler`, `app.py`, `web/`): validation, response, render. No scrape URLs or HTML parsers here.
- Price/discount logic stays in `server.py` helpers. Do not parse raw Flask/HTTP request objects inside scrape functions.
- Fetch/parse of Minfin and network sites: IO + parse only. Do **not** add a client/repository layer for one implementation.

## SOLID, coupling, patterns

- One reason to change per function.
- Abstraction only when a **second** implementation exists.
- Do not add Observer, DI containers, or “enterprise” folders.

## Performance

- Scrape in parallel where already patterned. Do not add sequential per-station HTTP on the request path.
- Hosted `/api/state` uses a fresh cache; full scrape only when stale or `/api/refresh`.
- Do not load unbounded HTML into extra in-memory copies of the same page.

## Reliability / security

- No empty `except`. Expected errors → keep last cache / HTTP message; unexpected → log and fail.
- Validate discount edits (known partner ids, fuel keys, numeric range). Never scrape Plusy “до X” as per-grade cuts.
- On hosted, never disable TLS verification. Never commit `.env` or wipe `data/discounts.local.json`.
- Logs: no tokens, no raw `.env`. Hosted API errors are generic, not stack traces.

## Maintainability

- Names describe purpose. If a paragraph of comments is needed, refactor.
- **Boy scout only in files already in the task diff.** Minimal diff wins over a cleaner-looking rewrite.
